  "summary": "Malicious code in vellutts (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (1ce772257825bac5182114b520a266d4541d9fc558388c1b845d48ec0cc629b1)\nNo install-time, import-time, or runtime behavior in this package version indicates exfiltration, remote code execution, credential access, silent relay, backdoor, or self-propagation. No lifecycle hooks fetching remote content, no reads of installer-secret paths, and no hardcoded attacker-controlled destinations were observed in the shipped files.\n\n## Source: kam193 (a36ed984afc7ca3475fe4852ef18158dc5569b049a35f4a23fd9260dc342c795)\nThis campaign consists of similar loader packages, which provide executing code from a given URL. While they do not contain the malicious payload and the usage remains unknown, they are clearly a coordinated campaign to place multiple deceptive ways to load malicious code.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-voice-synthesis-profiles\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n\n\n - other\n",
